> [!proposal] **Convert Tasks into a Semantically Linked Checklist**  
> **Explanation:** The current list of tasks is loosely organized. By converting them into a semantically linked checklist—with statuses (e.g., No Status, Todo, Completed) and tags (e.g., #backlog)—we can ensure that all task objects are interconnected. This will help in tracking dependencies, changes, and updates over time, even if some tasks move or change.  
> **Sample Fragment:**  
> ```markdown
> ### Task Checklist
> - [ ] **[!task] Create 'LITERATE BOOTSTRAP SPECIFICATIONS.md'**
>   - Add VIM notes and describe operations.
>   - Tags: #bootstrap, #backlog
> 
> - [ ] **[!task] Create 'LITERATE LANGUAGE SPECIFICATIONS.md'**
>   - Define vocabulary and structure elements.
>   - Tags: #language, #backlog
> 
> - [ ] **[!task] Create 'LITERATE DESIGN.md'**
>   - Link to Abstract Compositional Topology for Theory <-> Implementation mapping.
>   - Tags: #design
> ```  
> **Status:** Rejected

